Short:        Z offset setup helper for OctoPrint/Marlin
Author:       Denis Costils, with help from ChatGPT/Codex
Uploader:     Denis Costils
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      0.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.x, bsdsocket.library/AmiTCP compatible stack, OctoPrint API key
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

ZSetup is a small command line helper used to adjust the Z offset of a
Marlin printer controlled through OctoPrint.

It was written for a Tina2S/Marlin printer, after testing these commands:
G29, M420 S1, M851 Z..., M500 and M503.

Configuration
-------------

ZSetup uses the same OctoPrint configuration file as OctoControlSpeak:

  S:octocontrol_native.cfg

The file must contain your OctoPrint IP address, port and API key.

ZSetup stores its own current Z offset in:

  S:zsetup.cfg

The value is stored in centi-mm. For example OFFSET=-75 means -0.75 mm.

Usage
-----

First set the current known printer offset. For distribution, ZSetup starts
from 0.00 by default for safety:

  ZSetup SET OFFSET=0.00

Start the assisted setup:

  ZSetup START

This sends:

  G28
  G29
  M420 S1
  G90
  G1 Z10 F300
  G1 X50 Y50 F3000
  G1 Z0.5 F100

Then place a sheet of paper under the nozzle.

Move the nozzle down by 0.05 mm and save the new offset:

  ZSetup DOWN

Move the nozzle up by 0.05 mm and save the new offset:

  ZSetup UP

Show the saved ZSetup value:

  ZSetup SHOW

Return the printer to home:

  ZSetup HOME

Force saving the current ZSetup value to the printer:

  ZSetup SAVE

Safety
------

Keep your hand near the printer stop/power button while testing.
Use small steps only. This tool changes the printer Z offset with M851 and
saves it with M500.
Do not use this tool unless you understand the correct Z-offset direction for
your printer. A wrong Z-offset can make the nozzle hit the bed.

ZSetup refuses offsets outside this range:

  -5.00 mm to +5.00 mm

You can verify the real printer value from OctoPrint with:

  M503

Look for:

  M851 X0.00 Y0.00 Z-...
